<!--
    decbench campaign case O2-noinline-iproute2-ip-__get_hz (NOVEL pool: the
    emitted C stores into a .rodata string literal on a path where the binary
    performs no store at all).

    P3 simplification quiescence, cleanup pool.  SplitDatatype::splitCopy
    (upstream subflow.cc:2728, driven by RuleSplitCopy in the cleanup pool)
    splits a COPY whose data-type has components into one COPY per element.
    Its gate, SplitDatatype::testCopyConstraints (subflow.cc:2390), declines a
    copy whose input and output are address-tied at the SAME address, which is
    what a heritage return-copy is.

    Heritage::guardReturns inserts, before every RETURN, a synthetic
    `glob = glob` COPY for each persistent global so the global's final value
    stays live past the end of the function.  It is address-tied at one address
    on both sides, so the gate declines it and Merge::markInternalCopies then
    hides it from the printer.

    kuna's ActionStripStackGuard (option stackguard, DIV-14, default on) strips
    the stack-protector epilogue, which leaves a bare-epilogue RETURN block
    that ActionReturnSplit node-splits.  CloneBlockOps::cloneBlock rebuilds the
    block's ops through buildOpClone (whose flag mask does not carry
    return_copy) and patchInputs re-inputs the clone from a fresh COPY, so the
    cloned return-copy is neither marked return_copy nor address-tied at its
    own address, and the gate lets it through.  The split then produces one
    one-byte COPY per array element, each landing in a different HighVariable,
    so markInternalCopies can no longer hide them and P9 prints

        s_92e50[0xf] = SUB81(s_92e50[8],7);

    which is a store into .rodata.  The whole binary contains exactly ONE
    instruction that references 0x92e50 and it is the `movdqa` load; .rodata
    is flagged A, not W.

    Fix: testCopyConstraints declines when the COPY's OUTPUT varnode is
    read-only.  A store into a read-only range is never something the program
    performs, so this is a correctness fix and needs no option (DIV-55 in
    docs/history.md; it is a divergence from upstream subflow.cc:2390, whose
    precondition here is kuna's own stackguard divergence).

    Bytes: iproute2 `ip`, -O2 -fno-inline, function __get_hz at 0x6cbf0 (433
    bytes, verbatim), plus the 32-byte read-only literal at 0x92e50 that the
    16-byte `movdqa 0x260c8(%rip)` at 0x6cd8b loads.  The callees are PLT stubs
    outside the chunk and render as unnamed sub functions, exactly as they do
    in the full ELF.  `map addr` stands in for the strings analysis pass (which
    does not run on a bytechunk image): it plants the same typelocked char[32]
    the pass plants at a detected literal, and inherits the chunk's readonly
    property.

    Pass 1 is the default (the fix).  Pass 2 sets `option togglerule splitcopy
    off`, the rule's own name in the action pool, to pin the reference
    rendering in which no copy is split at all.
-->
